{
  "id": "COMPOUND:26652 - PROTEIN:4972",
  "verbalization": "Psammaplin D is implicated in the relationship with LAMA-84 through a series of molecular interactions involving Fucosyltransferase 9. This enzyme is a target of multiple compounds, including Psammaplin D, which is shown to inhibit Fucosyltransferase 9. The inhibition of Fucosyltransferase 9 leads to the activation of (1R,2R,3S,6E,8R,10S)-6,10-dimethyl-3-propan-2-yl-11-oxabicyclo[8.1.0]undec-6-ene-2,8-diol, which in turn targets LAMA-84. Similarly, Psammaplin D also inhibits Fucosyltransferase 9, which is a target of trans-5-Dodecen-7-yne and Semiplenamide A, both of which also target LAMA-84. The consistent involvement of Fucosyltransferase 9 as a common intermediate in the pathways leading to LAMA-84 suggests a potential mechanism where Psammaplin D exerts its effect by modulating the activity of this enzyme, thereby influencing the downstream pathway that leads to LAMA-84. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Psammaplin D and LAMA-84 through the inhibition of Fucosyltransferase 9, with the downstream targets of this enzyme playing a critical role in the relationship.",
